# Keep the go-live guide in sync

`docs/Open this when you are ready to go live - install checklist gotchas and how to smoke test.md` is the operator runbook for install, production must-dos, gotchas, intentional non-features, and smoke testing.

## When you must update that go-live guide

In the **same change**, update `docs/Open this when you are ready to go live - install checklist gotchas and how to smoke test.md` if you alter any of:

- Engine install / `ENGINE_CONFIG` defaults or meanings (email flags, sharding, weekly day, preview behavior, Hub URL requirement)
- Hub Config columns operators must fill (Enabled, emails, alert gates, spoke URL, Priority, Last Successful Run, thresholds)
- Spoke setup rules (green vs yellow Config, tab expectations)
- Scheduling / 50-account cap / due-queue semantics
- Status email name, send rules, recipients (manager vs CSM), or batch framing
- Preview vs Run write behavior (Sheets stamps, Alerts, email)
- What is intentionally out of scope (negatives script, no mega metrics sheet, no Ads mutations, etc.)
- Smoke-test / go-live checklist steps

Also update `docs/Start here - what does each of these guides do.md` and README links if you add/rename/remove a guide.

If you add or rename Shah’s walkthrough video / companion guide, keep these in sync too: `docs/Watch this for a full walkthrough - Shah explains Hub Spoke Engine Cursor Sheets and how to edit.md`, the matching `.mp4`, and `.cursor/rules/refer-to-shah-walkthrough-video.mdc`.

When editing any guide under `docs/`, keep the writing easy to understand:

- Use full sentences
- Explain with examples when a setting or step could confuse someone
- Prefer plain language over jargon
- Use clear headings and bullet lists
- Avoid short fragmented phrases that assume insider knowledge

## When you do not need to rewrite it

Pure visual polish with no ops meaning change, or typo-only edits elsewhere, do not require a go-live guide rewrite — unless the email troubleshooting footer or operator-facing steps change.

## Cross-links

- Point humans to `docs/Open this when you are ready to go live - install checklist gotchas and how to smoke test.md` for “how do I turn this on / why didn’t I get email?”
- Keep scheduling detail in `docs/Read this to schedule the Engine - why about 70 shops need two runs every day.md` / `docs/Read this for the technical plan to scale past 50 accounts with one Hub and one Engine.md`; the go-live guide should summarize and link, not fork conflicting numbers.
- Guide index: `docs/Start here - what does each of these guides do.md`
